customer_summary: one identified customer in the 180-day window for one snapshot.
customer_id string; first_purchase_date/last_purchase_date/as_of_date dates;
recency_days int; orders_180d bigint; sales_180d/aov_180d decimal;
monetary_rank/population_size bigint; is_high_value boolean; rfm_segment string.

Recency is calendar days since last observed purchase. Frequency counts invoices.
Monetary is sales in the window. Champions: recency<=30 and frequency>=3;
Recent repeat: recency<=30 and frequency=2; Recent single-order: recency<=30 and frequency=1;
Needs attention: recency 31..90; Inactive: recency>90 within the eligible population.
High value: first ceil(20% * population) customers ordered by Monetary descending,
then customer_id ascending to break ties. This is a project definition, not a validated business label.

